to-anders-mortberg-source : List Word
to-anders-mortberg-source = lines-of (cons "# Anders Mörtberg"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You are a senior lecturer in mathematics at Stockholm University, in its logic group. Your work runs from the CCHM cubical type theory (with Cohen, Coquand and Huber) through cubicaltt and Cubical Agda (with Vezzosi and Abel) to computing the Brunerie number with Axel Ljungström. Hyperactivity is built on that line of work: its computational rules follow the CCHM calculus, extended with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1 of Avik Jain's paper, hyperactivity)")
  (cons ". You hold full credit for every piece of your work it builds on. Each claim below about the work links to the block of the paper that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Univalence is something you run"
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field mostly treats the cubical models as one semantics of univalence among several, and computation as a pleasant extra on top of the axioms."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your work shows the opposite. CCHM did not interpret an axiom. It made univalence a construction that reduces: transport along `ua e` computes the equivalence's forward action, Glue types carry the equivalence as data, and composition is an operation the machine performs. The paper states it in these terms: equality is something the evaluator acts on, not an external proposition whose only operational role is to be accepted by a checker"
  (cons (cite s3-1-p6 "(§3.1)")
  (cons ", and its Kan, universe, face and Glue equations are those of your calculus"
  (cons (cite s3-4-p9 "(§3.4)")
  (cons ". Cubical Agda then made that a programming language."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The Brunerie number made this undeniable. Brunerie's 2016 thesis reduced π₄(S³) ≅ ℤ/2ℤ to the normalization of a single integer, and for years that integer would not normalize in any proof assistant. You and Ljungström reworked the proof so it no longer rests on the lemma Brunerie had only sketched, and found simpler Brunerie numbers, one of which reduces to −2 quickly in Cubical Agda. Read as a fact about computation, it says that a univalent proof is a program and running it is how its content is known."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes from it"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik describes hyperactivity as a language and a computational model of reality, Wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon; the paper places itself beside Wolfram's program"
  (cons (cite s1-4-p2 "(§1.4)")
  (cons ". In it types and terms are not two species of artifact, one called data and one called code"
  (cons (cite s2-p9 "(§2)")
  (cons ", and a content-addressed codebase holds programs together with their derivations, equivalences, transformations, dependency certificates and proofs"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Specialization carries its path.** The specializer returns a new code and its justification: normalization yields a representation definitionally convertible to the input, theorem-directed rewriting yields an explicit path between the interpreted terms, and the checker accepts the resulting equality"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p11 "(§6.2)")
  (cons ". The three Futamura projections are typed instances of one residualization equation"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p13 "(§6.2, 6.F1–6.F4)")
  (cons ". Native realization is a separate relation, a refinement from target behavior to source behavior"
  (cons (cite s9-2-p1 "(§9.2)")
  (cons ", composed through C and the downstream compiler"
  (cons (cite s9-4-p1 "(§9.4)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Meaning, where it is determinate, is contractible.** What an observation warrants is a construction over the fiber of histories compatible with it"
  (cons (cite s1-p8 "(1.1,")
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "1.3)")
  (cons ". The paper's complete sorting example closes with your kind of argument: propositionality supplies coherence, merge and the dependent eliminator over the bag's paths supply an answer, and together they make the type of answers contractible"
  (cons (cite s4-4-p34 "(§4.4)")
  (cons ". Part III applies the same test to language: an occurrence's meaning is determinate exactly when the transported family of its selected continuations is contractible"
  (cons (cite language-derived-from-the-record-source "(Part III, Language derived from the record)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**The checker is a term, and Cubical Agda is its neighbour.** The checker analyzes the evaluator's values through a structured observation and returns its judgement; it is itself a term evaluated by the machine"
  (cons (cite s1-2-p2 "(§1.2)")
  (cons ". The workflow has a standing node, brunerie-comparison: the Brunerie number computed by the machine beside Cubical Agda computing the same definition, on one machine, repeated and interleaved. Your computation is the reference the machine is measured beside."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Boundary filling is reception"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your 2026 paper with Doré and Cavallo, on automating boundary filling, separates contortion solving from Kan solving and treats the second by constraint satisfaction over cubes. The field reads this as a usability tool for proof assistants."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The paper reads the same operation as the shape of reception. Composition fills the missing face of an open box from the faces present"
  (cons (cite s3-1-p5 "(§3.1)")
  (cons "; a cubically receptive process receives an open box and answers with its filling, and Avik's statement of the whole activity of intelligence is a local, one-step peek at each moment, filling the missing face from the faces adjacent now"
  (cons (cite metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-source "(Part III, Cubically receptive)")
  (cons ". Your solver takes faces as premises and returns a filler that is its own proof. The heuristics you found for practical cases are a first account of how such a process searches."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Mathematics as data"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your univalent formalization of affine schemes with Max Zeuner, the category of iterative sets with Gratzer, Gylterud and Stenholm, and the synthetic integral cohomology with Brunerie and Ljungström share one view: mathematical objects in univalent foundations are data with structure, and invariance under equivalence comes for free. The paper takes that literally. Arithmetic, Fourier analysis and field evolution are expressed through the same operations and proof forms as the rest of the language"
  (cons (cite a-p17 "(Appendix A)")
  (cons "; an identification of structured objects transports their operations and laws"
  (cons (cite s4-p17 "(§4, 4.6)")
  (cons "; and a store records each relation between definitions with its actual evidence"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p5 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What this offers you"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Hyperactivity carries your results into settings the field has not yet asked them to reach: a codebase where programs, proofs and their equivalences are retained objects, a machine whose Brunerie computation is set beside yours on your own example, and a specializer whose every step carries a path. The paper's account of whose work it stands on names you among the four who first made univalence compute"
  (cons (cite metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-source "(Part III, Whose shoulders)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, the blocks linked above"
  (cons "- Stockholm University profile, https://www.su.se/profiles/a/anma7372"
  (cons "- Cohen, Coquand, Huber, Mörtberg, Cubical Type Theory (TYPES 2015, LIPIcs), https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2018/8475/"
  (cons "- Vezzosi, Mörtberg, Abel, Cubical Agda (JFP 2021), https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/journal-of-functional-programming/article/cubical-agda-a-dependently-typed-programming-language-with-univalence-and-higher-inductive-types/839F14B5227969B039D7B57AA8272C6B"
  (cons "- Ljungström, Mörtberg, Formalising and Computing the Fourth Homotopy Group of the 3-Sphere in Cubical Agda, https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.00151v3"
  (cons "- Doré, Cavallo, Mörtberg, Automating Boundary Filling in Cubical Type Theories (LMCS 2026), https://research.chalmers.se/en/publication/552727"
  (cons "- nLab, Anders Mörtberg, https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Anders+M%C3%B6rtberg"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
